---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { graph, organizationSchema } from '../lib/schema';

export const prerender = true;

const schema = graph([organizationSchema()]);
---

<Layout
  title="About Meridian"
  description="Meridian is a specialist firm that measures where B2B buyers discover vendors during research — across Google and AI search. Founded by Jeremy Nelson."
  structuredData={schema}
>
  <header class="bg-dark text-on-dark pt-28 pb-16 md:pt-36 md:pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-dark">The firm</p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-display text-4xl leading-[1.05] md:text-6xl">
        Built to measure the research that happens before a sales conversation.
      </h1>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="bg-paper py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      <p>
        Meridian exists because buyer research moved and most measurement did not. Teams still report on traffic, rankings, and campaigns. Meanwhile a shortlist can form in an AI answer or a Google snapshot that never touches the website those reports describe.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell "AI SEO." We sell visibility during buyer research: which questions can turn into revenue, who is named when those questions are asked, and which sources put a competitor in the room instead of you.
      </p>
      <p>
        The commercial offer is narrow on purpose. A 30-day Sprint. Then, only if the evidence supports it, a monthly Monitor with no annual contract. If there isn't a meaningful opportunity, we say so.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-[0.7fr_1.3fr]">
      <p class="eyebrow">Founder</p>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl">{SITE.founder}</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          <p>
            Jeremy Nelson founded Meridian after years of measuring what companies believed they were doing in search against what buyers actually saw. The gap was rarely a missing blog post. It was a missing answer at the moment a buyer described a job, a risk, or a comparison.
          </p>
          <p>
            His work sits on the measurement side of marketing: isolate the question, record the answer, explain the source, report the miss without theater. He runs client Sprints himself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-dark text-on-dark py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl">How we work</h2>
      <ul class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-on-dark-muted leading-relaxed">
        <li class="border-t border-white/15 pt-5"><strong class="text-on-dark">Show the evidence.</strong> Recommendations come with the question, the occupancy, and the source. We do not ask you to trust a score.</li>
        <li class="border-t border-white/15 pt-5"><strong class="text-on-dark">Stay on revenue questions.</strong> We do not expand the prompt list to look busy. Discover, Evaluate, Compare, Validate, Buy.</li>
        <li class="border-t border-white/15 pt-5"><strong class="text-on-dark">Tell you when to stop.</strong> If you already occupy the answers that matter, that is the finding.</li>
      </ul>
      <a href="/#missing" class="btn btn-primary mt-10" data-track="cta_see_where_click" data-location="about">See where you're missing</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
